cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reproducibility artifacts, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LearnFlow: A K12 Gamified Adaptive Learning Platform and Measurement Instrument for Learning-Addiction Research"
abstract: >-
  LearnFlow is a K12 gamified adaptive-learning platform released primarily as a reproducible
  research artifact for the study of learning addiction. Its measurement contribution is a
  dual-source, five-dimension framework that combines behavioural logs (durations, night-time
  ratio, hint dependence) with a self-report instrument layer covering the dimensions logs
  structurally cannot observe: behavioural control, sleep and social impairment, and
  time-perception bias. Unmeasured dimensions are excluded from the index weighting and
  reported through an explicit coverage object rather than silently scored as healthy. The
  artifact also accompanies empirical work on the commensurability of difficulty scales,
  external-validity testing of the 85% success-rate rule, ordered-action bandits with a
  formalised flow channel, and reliability boundaries of LLM-based difficulty annotation.
  Every headline count in the documentation is recomputed from source by scripts under
  learnflow-backend/scripts/, and the consistency check fails loudly when a documented number
  diverges from the code.
